      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are there any cases where we need both of these? Would it be better to just have thread-\u003eee and get rid of the local? If you like the conciseness of \"ee\", you could have a local pointer and then set it here as:\n\n  ee \u003d \u0026thread-\u003eee;\n  \nThere\u0027s also a third copy (e-\u003eee) that looks like it isn\u0027t initialized anywhere in the non-error case. It seems like we don\u0027t need three copies of it.",
