      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T02:25:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previous patches keep a single copy as suggested: `ee \u003d \u0026thread-\u003eee;`. However, this became a problem when populating the error on the target thread, as it\u0027s also accessed from a different thread/process.\n\nFor this reason I went back to the 3 copies (local, thread and transaction log) which is what the driver currently uses.\n\nI suppose there are other alternatives as locking during each `binder_set_extended_error()` or maybe reusing the `transaction_log-\u003eee` instead of the local `ee`. I doubt those are better solutions though.",
      "parentUuid": "4cecedcd_cb1646b4",
      "revId": "d9ef038cc6f058027275669b8c5c4c0275d1fcc3",
